<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-855] LuceneTextValueEncoder doesn&apos;t properly set internal buffers, causing BufferUnderflowException</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-855</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The LuceneTextValueEncoder throws an BufferUnderflowException when used.  See the code below.  The problem appears to be due to the CharBuffer not getting values, but I&apos;m not sure yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;@Test
  &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void testLucene() &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception {
    LuceneTextValueEncoder enc = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; LuceneTextValueEncoder(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;text&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
    enc.setAnalyzer(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; WhitespaceAnalyzer(Version.LUCENE_34));
    Vector v1 = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; DenseVector(200);
    enc.addToVector(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;test1 and more&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, v1);
    enc.flush(1, v1);
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here&apos;s the exception:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;java.nio.BufferUnderflowException&lt;br/&gt;
	at java.nio.HeapCharBuffer.get(HeapCharBuffer.java:127)&lt;br/&gt;
	at org.apache.mahout.vectorizer.encoders.LuceneTextValueEncoder$CharSequenceReader.read(LuceneTextValueEncoder.java:87)&lt;br/&gt;
	at org.apache.lucene.analysis.CharReader.read(CharReader.java:54)&lt;br/&gt;
	at org.apache.lucene.util.CharacterUtils$Java5CharacterUtils.fill(CharacterUtils.java:181)&lt;br/&gt;
